==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|scrutinium||a search, an inquiry}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|scrutari||to search or examine thoroughly, probably originally to search among rubbish}} < {{term|scruta||rubbish, broken trash}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈskɹuː.tɪ.niː/}}, {{SAMPA|/"skru:.tI.ni:/}}
* {{hyphenation|scru|ti|ny}}
* {{audio|en-us-scrutiny.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|scrutin|ies}}

# Intense [[study]] of someone or something.
# Thorough [[inspection]] of a situation or a case.

